WEBVTT

00:03.880 --> 00:04.240
All right.

00:04.240 --> 00:09.600
So now what we're going to do, we're going to go and modify and manipulate your data inside the database.

00:09.600 --> 00:11.040
So now sometimes what happens.

00:11.040 --> 00:14.240
You have a table inside your database and the table is empty.

00:14.280 --> 00:16.840
You don't have any rows any data inside the table.

00:16.880 --> 00:22.040
Now in order to add your data to the table what you can do you can use the command inserts.

00:22.040 --> 00:25.760
So insert going to go and add a new rows to your table.

00:25.800 --> 00:26.800
And of course not always.

00:26.800 --> 00:27.920
The table must be empty.

00:27.920 --> 00:34.280
To add your data, you can add new rows to already existing data, and SQL can go and append it at the

00:34.280 --> 00:35.040
end of the table.

00:35.040 --> 00:40.440
Now my friends, in order to insert a new data to the target table, there are two methods the first

00:40.440 --> 00:41.480
and the classical way.

00:41.520 --> 00:47.560
In order to insert new data, we can use the insert command and manually specifying the values that

00:47.560 --> 00:49.240
should be inserted to the table.

00:49.240 --> 00:52.200
So you're going to start specifying in the script the values.

00:52.200 --> 00:55.760
And then they're going to be inserted as new rows to the target table.

00:55.760 --> 01:01.840
So in this process you are manually inserting new values to the table using like an SQL scripts.

01:01.880 --> 01:04.670
So now we're going to focus on this scenario on how to insert data.

01:04.710 --> 01:05.110
All right.

01:05.150 --> 01:07.790
Now let's check quickly the syntax of the insert command.

01:07.830 --> 01:09.990
Let's start with the keyword insert into.

01:10.030 --> 01:12.390
And after that we have to specify the table name.

01:12.390 --> 01:13.710
So where we want to insert.

01:13.710 --> 01:17.670
And then we make a list of all columns that we want to insert.

01:17.670 --> 01:21.990
And then we specify a list of columns where we're going to insert values into them.

01:21.990 --> 01:23.790
And after that we say values.

01:23.790 --> 01:28.430
And finally we're going to go now and specify the data that should be inserted to the table.

01:28.470 --> 01:31.790
And we make it as well as a list like we have done for the columns.

01:31.830 --> 01:36.510
Now in the insert statements specifying those columns it is totally optional.

01:36.510 --> 01:43.030
So if you don't specify the columns of the table, then SQL can expect you to insert values into each

01:43.030 --> 01:43.470
column.

01:43.470 --> 01:47.110
Because sometimes, of course, we don't want to insert value for each column.

01:47.110 --> 01:52.110
You can skip few columns, of course, but if you want to insert a value for each column, either you

01:52.110 --> 01:55.030
go and specify them as a list or you can skip it.

01:55.070 --> 02:00.550
Now for the insert statements, there is a very important rule the number of columns and values must

02:00.550 --> 02:01.110
match.

02:01.110 --> 02:06.740
So if you specify here three columns then you must insert as well exactly three values.

02:06.740 --> 02:08.300
So this must be matching.

02:08.340 --> 02:10.340
And one last thing about the syntax.

02:10.340 --> 02:12.940
You can insert multiple values in one go.

02:12.940 --> 02:17.140
So for each row you can specify a list of values that must be inserted.

02:17.140 --> 02:18.620
So that's all about the syntax.

02:18.620 --> 02:22.260
Let's go back to SQL in order to practice insert commands.

02:22.420 --> 02:24.460
So now let's go and insert a new customers.

02:24.460 --> 02:25.340
So it's very simple.

02:25.340 --> 02:27.500
Let's start with insert into.

02:27.540 --> 02:30.460
So we are saying we want to insert data into.

02:30.460 --> 02:33.100
So we have to go and specify the table name customers.

02:33.140 --> 02:37.860
Now after that we have to specify a list of columns where we want to insert data into it.

02:37.900 --> 02:38.620
And what we can do.

02:38.620 --> 02:41.740
We can go and check which columns do we have inside our table.

02:41.740 --> 02:46.020
So we can see we have ID first name country score, and we can go and make a list of that.

02:46.020 --> 02:51.460
So we can say ID first name country and score.

02:51.860 --> 02:54.900
So we just have a list of all columns inside our table.

02:54.900 --> 02:55.700
Customers.

02:55.740 --> 02:58.020
Now what we need we need the values.

02:58.020 --> 02:59.580
So which data should be inserted.

02:59.580 --> 03:01.460
So we can go and open two parenthesis.

03:01.500 --> 03:03.220
And now we have to specify an ID.

03:03.260 --> 03:05.180
We know the last customer was five.

03:05.180 --> 03:07.060
So we're going to go with the customer sex.

03:07.060 --> 03:09.180
Now we have to give the name of the customer.

03:09.220 --> 03:12.100
Let's go for Anna and then a country.

03:12.140 --> 03:13.420
Let's go for USA.

03:13.620 --> 03:15.940
And this customer has no scores.

03:15.980 --> 03:17.740
So what we can do, we can say null.

03:17.740 --> 03:20.100
So we don't know the score of this customer.

03:20.140 --> 03:22.500
Nulls means nothing we don't know.

03:22.500 --> 03:24.700
So with that you can go and insert one row.

03:24.700 --> 03:27.820
But now let's say that I would like to go and insert like a second row.

03:27.860 --> 03:28.820
One more customer.

03:28.860 --> 03:32.260
What we can do, we can separate this with a comma.

03:32.300 --> 03:34.820
And then we can go and repeat the whole thing again.

03:34.820 --> 03:36.100
So the ID is seven.

03:36.140 --> 03:38.780
The next one let's call this customer Sam.

03:38.780 --> 03:41.260
And we don't know the country of this customer.

03:41.260 --> 03:42.660
So we're going to say it's null.

03:42.700 --> 03:44.140
But the score we know it already.

03:44.180 --> 03:45.180
It is 100.

03:45.180 --> 03:47.980
So as you can see we are adding a value for each of those columns.

03:48.020 --> 03:52.300
And if you don't know the answer then make it null if the database allows it to be null.

03:52.340 --> 03:55.620
Some columns they are not allowed to be null like the primary key.

03:55.620 --> 03:58.820
So if you go say over here null, the database will not allow it.

03:58.860 --> 04:00.740
Well actually we can go and test it.

04:00.780 --> 04:01.740
Let's execute.

04:01.740 --> 04:05.460
And you can see you cannot insert the value null into the column ID.

04:05.460 --> 04:06.580
So this is not allowed.

04:06.580 --> 04:07.500
You can have a seven.

04:07.500 --> 04:09.530
But for the other columns it is allowed.

04:09.530 --> 04:11.570
You can go and check the definition of the table.

04:11.610 --> 04:13.530
Now we go and execute.

04:13.570 --> 04:18.570
Now the output of the modifications command is going to always indicate what happens to the data.

04:18.610 --> 04:21.170
So it says two rows affected.

04:21.210 --> 04:23.690
Affected might be inserted updated deleted.

04:23.690 --> 04:26.610
So you can get a general statement from the database.

04:26.610 --> 04:29.050
But you are getting how many record is affected.

04:29.050 --> 04:31.650
So we got two because we have inserted two records.

04:31.650 --> 04:33.930
So now as you can see it's not like the query.

04:33.970 --> 04:36.370
We are not getting any data in the output.

04:36.370 --> 04:37.730
We are just getting a message.

04:37.730 --> 04:43.250
So this is a big difference between querying the data, using the selects and modifying the data using

04:43.250 --> 04:43.730
inserts.

04:43.730 --> 04:47.930
We are doing now direct modifications to the data inside our database.

04:47.970 --> 04:52.690
Of course, if you want to see the data in the customers, what we can do, we can go and query the

04:52.690 --> 04:53.450
data, right.

04:53.690 --> 04:54.690
So let's go and do that.

04:54.690 --> 04:58.370
Select star from customers I would like to see the whole table.

04:58.370 --> 05:00.090
So mark it and execute it.

05:00.130 --> 05:02.250
Now you can see we have seven customers.

05:02.250 --> 05:04.050
So we just manipulated our data.

05:04.050 --> 05:05.810
We have here Anna and Sam.

05:05.850 --> 05:08.010
This is how you can insert data to the database.

05:08.010 --> 05:09.170
Now there is like few rules.

05:09.170 --> 05:13.960
You have to be careful As you are inserting new data to your tables, you have to pay attention that

05:13.960 --> 05:19.840
the order of the columns that you have defined insert is matching the values that you are inserting

05:19.840 --> 05:20.320
over here.

05:20.320 --> 05:21.240
Let's have an example.

05:21.240 --> 05:23.600
I'm going to go and remove this over here.

05:23.640 --> 05:26.000
And let's say that we are inserting a new one.

05:26.040 --> 05:26.760
Number eight.

05:26.800 --> 05:32.400
And now in the first name instead of the name of the customers, we have inserted the country like USA

05:32.520 --> 05:35.040
and in the country we have inserted the name.

05:35.040 --> 05:37.200
This is just a mistake and we are all human, right?

05:37.200 --> 05:38.600
So let's have a name like this.

05:38.600 --> 05:39.000
Max.

05:39.000 --> 05:43.640
Now if you go and execute it, the database can accept it because it is really hard for the database

05:43.640 --> 05:45.440
to understand that you have made here an error.

05:45.480 --> 05:49.600
Both of them are varchar and the database doesn't care about the content of the data.

05:49.640 --> 05:52.160
As long as you are following the rules of the data type.

05:52.160 --> 05:57.040
So now if you go and select the data from the customers, you can see now we have a customer called

05:57.080 --> 05:59.160
USA from the country Max.

05:59.160 --> 06:02.440
So the SQL going to do it blindly like you insert the data.

06:02.480 --> 06:06.400
As long as you are following the data type rules and the constraints.

06:06.400 --> 06:12.350
So for example, if you made this error over here and you say the ID is max and let's say the first

06:12.390 --> 06:16.030
name is let's say nine and you execute it here.

06:16.030 --> 06:18.030
The database is smart enough to say, you know what?

06:18.030 --> 06:19.030
There is something wrong.

06:19.070 --> 06:22.510
The ID should not be a string so the database can reject your inserts.

06:22.550 --> 06:24.710
Be careful of the order of your columns.

06:24.750 --> 06:26.710
Now let's go and query again our table.

06:26.750 --> 06:31.710
Now if you are in the insert commands defining all the columns exactly like the table.

06:31.710 --> 06:35.030
So as you can see we have here complete match ID first name country score.

06:35.030 --> 06:37.430
We have all the columns and as well the correct order.

06:37.470 --> 06:40.670
There is like lazy way you can go and remove the whole thing over here.

06:40.710 --> 06:46.070
And with that the database can understand okay we are inserting values to all of the columns so SQL

06:46.110 --> 06:46.750
can understand.

06:46.750 --> 06:50.550
You are inserting something to each columns in the correct direction.

06:50.550 --> 06:53.110
So let's go and do that correctly nine.

06:53.110 --> 06:55.910
And here let's say we have Andreas.

06:56.070 --> 06:57.830
Andreas is from Germany.

06:57.830 --> 07:02.510
So if you go and execute it it will be working even though we didn't define the columns.

07:02.510 --> 07:08.190
And that's because the values that we are inserting are exactly the same number of columns of the table

07:08.190 --> 07:09.670
and following as well the rules.

07:09.710 --> 07:14.630
Now moving on to the next one, you can go and add only two columns in the definition if you're not

07:14.630 --> 07:15.270
already.

07:15.270 --> 07:18.150
Always the country and the score is null.

07:18.190 --> 07:20.870
We know only two informations the id and the name.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.910
Then you don't have always to go and say null, null, null and so on.

07:23.910 --> 07:25.270
We can go and skip that.

07:25.310 --> 07:25.470
Okay.

07:25.510 --> 07:26.670
So now let me show you what I mean.

07:26.670 --> 07:32.030
We're going to go after the table name and we're going to define only two columns the ID and the first

07:32.070 --> 07:32.590
name.

07:32.590 --> 07:36.070
So that means we are telling SQL we want to insert only two columns.

07:36.110 --> 07:37.470
And now you have to be careful.

07:37.470 --> 07:41.470
If you define here two columns then the values should be as well two columns.

07:41.470 --> 07:44.270
So we can remove the country and the score.

07:44.270 --> 07:46.670
And we can go and add only two informations.

07:46.670 --> 07:49.710
So ten and we can go and add here for example Sarah.

07:49.830 --> 07:52.550
So if we go and execute it it will be working.

07:52.550 --> 07:55.990
And now what this skill is doing with the other two columns it's going to be nulls.

07:55.990 --> 07:58.190
So let's go and select again from our table.

07:58.190 --> 08:03.670
You can see here Sarah has null in the country and as well in the score because we didn't define those

08:03.670 --> 08:04.390
informations.

08:04.390 --> 08:05.110
But be careful.

08:05.110 --> 08:08.430
You cannot here skip a column that is not allowed to be null.

08:08.430 --> 08:12.470
So you have always to have in your list all the columns that are not null.

08:12.510 --> 08:15.070
So for example, I cannot go and insert only the first name.

08:15.070 --> 08:20.140
I will get an error because the database can try to insert a null in the ID and this is not allowed,

08:20.140 --> 08:22.940
so you can skip only nullable columns.

08:26.860 --> 08:27.780
All right my friends.

08:27.780 --> 08:31.820
So that was the first method on how to insert data to your target table.

08:31.860 --> 08:37.500
As you saw by typing manually the values inside an insert command using values.

08:37.540 --> 08:39.380
And now let's move to another method.

08:39.380 --> 08:42.420
We can insert data, but this time not manually.

08:42.420 --> 08:45.020
We can insert data using another table.

08:45.020 --> 08:46.780
So imagine we have the following scenario.

08:46.820 --> 08:49.500
We have an already existing table with data.

08:49.500 --> 08:52.380
And this is going to be the source table the source of your data.

08:52.380 --> 08:53.820
And we have another table.

08:53.820 --> 08:55.300
This table is empty.

08:55.300 --> 08:58.260
And we want to insert a new data to this target table.

08:58.300 --> 09:04.420
Now what we can do we can take the data from the source table and insert it into the target table without

09:04.420 --> 09:07.220
manually writing a script for the values.

09:07.220 --> 09:09.940
So we are moving the data from one table to another.

09:09.980 --> 09:12.660
Now, in order to do that, we need to do two steps.

09:12.660 --> 09:18.130
The first step we have to write an SQL query using select from, and so on.

09:18.130 --> 09:22.090
In order to select the data that we need from the source table.

09:22.090 --> 09:24.530
And once you do that, you will get the results.

09:24.530 --> 09:27.010
So this is like you are doing a normal query.

09:27.050 --> 09:30.130
You write select and you will get an answer with the results.

09:30.170 --> 09:32.250
And now what we can do in the next step.

09:32.250 --> 09:39.210
We can take these results and use an insert command in order to insert this results into the target

09:39.250 --> 09:39.770
table.

09:39.770 --> 09:43.610
And with that, we have moved the data from the source table to the target table.

09:43.610 --> 09:47.330
So first write the query on the source table and the second step.

09:47.330 --> 09:50.570
Use an insert to move this result to the target table.

09:50.570 --> 09:52.850
So let's go back to SQL in order to do that.

09:52.850 --> 09:53.970
So now we have the following task.

09:53.970 --> 09:58.370
And it says insert data from the table customers into the table persons.

09:58.370 --> 10:03.570
So that means the source table is the customers and the target table is persons.

10:03.650 --> 10:09.250
Now how I usually do it is that I keep my eye on the target table to understand the structure of this

10:09.250 --> 10:13.850
table, and I start writing the query from the source table.

10:13.850 --> 10:18.330
If you go to the left side, you can see okay, we have here an ID, we have here person name, birth

10:18.330 --> 10:19.090
date and phone.

10:19.090 --> 10:22.800
And you can see only the birth date except nulls and the rest.

10:22.800 --> 10:24.560
We have always to provide informations.

10:24.560 --> 10:27.760
So with that I have now understanding about the table persons.

10:27.800 --> 10:31.080
Now next I'm going to go and start writing the query from the source.

10:31.080 --> 10:32.560
So we start like this.

10:32.560 --> 10:37.320
Select star from our table customers just to have an overview of our table.

10:37.360 --> 10:43.880
Now the next step we're going to go and design a perfect result from this query that is matching the

10:43.880 --> 10:44.800
target table.

10:44.800 --> 10:48.120
So in the output we need ID and we have it from the customer.

10:48.120 --> 10:51.160
From the original table we're going to go and select ID okay.

10:51.200 --> 10:53.600
So now next we need a person name.

10:53.600 --> 10:56.480
And here we have from the original table something called first name.

10:56.480 --> 10:58.240
So this is a perfect match.

10:58.240 --> 11:01.480
So we're going to go and select this table as a second column.

11:01.480 --> 11:03.000
So we have covered the first two.

11:03.040 --> 11:05.080
Then the third one is going to be the birth date.

11:05.080 --> 11:09.640
Well my friends we don't have birth dates but the database can accept it as a null.

11:09.640 --> 11:14.120
So I'm going to go and write a null because I don't have such information from the source table.

11:14.160 --> 11:16.200
And now the next one is going to be the phone as well.

11:16.200 --> 11:21.080
We don't have phone informations, but we cannot have it as a null because it says here not null.

11:21.080 --> 11:24.240
So what we're going to do, we're going to go and add a static value.

11:24.280 --> 11:25.200
A default value.

11:25.200 --> 11:27.400
So we're going to have two single quotes.

11:27.400 --> 11:29.400
And in between we're going to say unknown.

11:29.600 --> 11:32.360
Since it is Varchar it can accept these words.

11:32.360 --> 11:34.600
So now let's go and just query.

11:34.600 --> 11:37.320
So we have the ID we have the first name.

11:37.320 --> 11:40.640
The birth date is empty and the font is unknown.

11:40.680 --> 11:45.600
Now you might say, but the column name is not matching with the column name of the persons.

11:45.600 --> 11:51.680
Well, the database does not care about that as long as the result of the data is matching the table,

11:51.720 --> 11:53.120
it can go and insert it.

11:53.120 --> 11:56.240
So the database will never compare the column names together.

11:56.240 --> 12:02.040
But if you like and go and add here like the aliases, exactly like the target table, it will not hurt,

12:02.040 --> 12:04.280
but it has no effect on the results.

12:04.280 --> 12:04.920
All right okay.

12:04.960 --> 12:07.800
So now we have like query selects and we have a results.

12:07.800 --> 12:09.480
But this is not an insert.

12:09.480 --> 12:12.760
So how are we going to insert the result of this into the table.

12:12.800 --> 12:13.400
Persons.

12:13.400 --> 12:17.520
Well for that we need the insert into commands.

12:17.520 --> 12:18.760
So insert into.

12:18.960 --> 12:22.720
And now we have to specify the target table can be the persons.

12:22.760 --> 12:28.030
And of course you can go and list all the column names, but if you have like exact match, you can

12:28.030 --> 12:28.390
skip it.

12:28.390 --> 12:32.990
But for me, I would like always to add it just to make sure that we don't have any issue.

12:33.030 --> 12:36.910
So the ID person name, birth date and the phone.

12:38.430 --> 12:39.550
So that's it.

12:39.590 --> 12:41.350
Let's go and execute.

12:41.350 --> 12:42.430
So it is working.

12:42.430 --> 12:44.430
Now we can see ten rows affected.

12:44.430 --> 12:50.830
Well that means ten rows are inserted from the table customers into the target persons.

12:50.870 --> 12:55.990
And now what we can do we can go and query the table persons just to check that everything is working

12:55.990 --> 12:56.790
perfectly.

12:57.110 --> 13:00.550
Select star from persons and let's go and execute.

13:00.590 --> 13:04.830
And with that you can see our ten persons that we have added from the customers.

13:04.830 --> 13:09.710
So with that we have moved the data from one table and inserted into another table.

13:09.750 --> 13:11.510
And as you can see it was very simple.

13:11.510 --> 13:17.070
First you have to write a query from the source table in order to collect the data that you need.

13:17.110 --> 13:20.750
And then you go and insert it into the target table.

13:20.750 --> 13:22.430
So this is really nice and easy.

13:22.470 --> 13:26.230
And this is another way on how to insert data into your database.
